--- REGISTRATION (2026-09-06, before any sweep) ---

Objective: a DEFAULT_PF config (no structural code change in phase
A) that raises posterior information capture on the frozen
scenarios without breaking the standing gates. Structural changes
only if the config frontier saturates (phase A2, separate
registration).

Phase A — offline sweep (post_sweep.py) scored against the STORED
ground-truth rows (results/post_s{1,2,3}_rows.jsonl; empirical
conditionals are data, re-used freely — re-slice, never re-run):
  Metrics per cfg per scenario: info captured % (Brier vs uniform
  vs achievable), M3 channel gaps, M4 deadwood gap.
  Staged grid: (1) tau_p x lik_floor on S1; (2) tau_d x mu x eps
  on S2/S3; (3) joint top-4 combos on all three.
  Overfitting guard: 3 scenarios is a TINY validation set — the
  sweep SELECTS, it does not confirm.
Phase B — held-out validation of the ONE selected cfg:
  (a) read_regress.py hold-or-sharpen (existing truth-keyed gate);
  (b) stream Brier held-out teacher+clone + random-opponent
      mismatch (particle.py _score_pf machinery) — must not
      regress materially (register: mismatch degradation < 5
      Brier-% vs champion);
  (c) TWO FRESH scenarios (S4/S5, picker seed 114000, run seeds
      116000/118000, ~1500 accepted each) sampled AFTER the cfg is
      chosen — posterior capture must improve vs DEFAULT_PF on
      these too (selection seed != confirmation seed, applied to
      scenarios).
Phase C — match gate (t2_gate pattern + pf_cfg pass-through in
  HomeV8Policy): candidate vs champion, 2000 paired deals, seed
  120000; fresh confirm 122000 if positive. Per the v7 promotion
  protocol a TIE promotes on posterior quality IF (a)-(c) all
  hold and the poison probe (ad_self, ad_jam) stays clean.
Seeds: 114000/116000/118000/120000/122000 (mod 977 = 668/714/760/
806/852, distinct from all used bases).

--- PHASE A RESULTS (2026-09-06): config frontier SATURATES ---

Sweep logs: results/v10_sweep_stage{1,2,3}.log. Champion baseline
capture s1/s2/s3 = 89.6/69.3/60.6% (mean 73.2%).
Stage 1 (S1): tau_p=0.0 wins decisively — capture 91.6%, opening
channel gap 0.179 -> 0.052; lik_floor irrelevant; exact zero is
numerically safe.
Stage 2 (S2/S3): SHARPENING tau_d BACKFIRES — s3 collapses 60.6 ->
40.1% at tau_d=0.75: the discard energy's softness was protecting
against its own misspecification; the discard-choice
counterfactual is NOT expressible by the current energy at any
temperature. eps 0.05->0.02 and mu 0.5 give crumbs.
Stage 3 (joint): best config tau_p=0.0 + eps=0.02 -> mean 74.6%
(91.6/70.1/62.1). Config-only gain +1.4 points of capture.
VERDICT: phase A2 (structural) triggered per registration. The
indicated change is the v7 take-side redesign applied to the
DISCARD side (HANDOFF_V8 frontier #4): discard_mode="rule" —
score P(discard X | hand) by the teacher's actual discard rule
(min dw-after, live/safe/value tie-breaks) with a calibrated
mismatch rate, behind a mode flag; v6/v7 frozen behavior
untouched (pickup_mode precedent).

--- PHASE A2 REGISTRATION (2026-09-06): structural discard fix ---

Root cause read from particle.SoftOpponent.discard_logprob: energy
= dw_after + mu*live(drop). Deadwood-tied discards (two dead high
cards) score ~50/50, but the deployment opponent tie-breaks
near-deterministically toward the higher-value/deader card — this
is the missing discard-choice counterfactual (S2: truth KS 0.099
vs PF 0.198 after a TH discard).
Candidates, smallest first, each behind a param/flag with frozen
default (pickup_mode precedent; v6/v7 registry behavior pinned):
  (a) nu: energy -= nu * DEADWOOD_VALUE[drop] (nu=0 = frozen).
      Sweep nu x tau_d on stored S2/S3 rows.
  (b) discard_mode="rule": exact teacher tie-broken argmin with
      mismatch rate, softmax fallback — only if (a) leaves the
      channel gaps standing.
Selection metric unchanged (capture % + channel gaps + dw gap on
stored rows); phase B unchanged and binding.

--- PHASE A2 RESULTS (2026-09-06): four structural discard
attempts, all negative; candidate selected ---

Sweep logs: results/v10_sweep_{nu,kdraw,sigma,tier,taupo}.log.
  nu (value tie-break term): fails — S3 collapses at every nu>0;
    the missing suppression is not the value tie-break.
  kdraw=31 (full draw marginalization): does NOT rescue sharp
    tau_d (S3 42.8%) — the subsample was not the cause.
  sigma (in-hand synergy term): helps S3 channels (1.10->0.83)
    but wrecks S2 (69.9->58.6 at sigma=2) — a single linear term
    cannot separate pair-breaking from junk-cluster shedding.
  discard_mode="tier" (two-scale argmin likelihood): S2 ground
    truth motivated it (observed discard in dw-argmin 100%/1500,
    teacher tie-break match only 23% ~ uniform-within) but S3
    collapses (62->32%): after a STOCK DRAW the search often dumps
    the drawn junk even when a bigger dead card sits in hand —
    argmin membership is context-dependent. All four negative
    results documented; the discard side needs a measured behavior
    model of the search (future campaign; likelihood-net territory
    — respect lessons #2/#8/#10).
  tau_po split (opening-only zero mismatch): scores ~= global
    tau_p=0 on the scenarios (74.3-74.5% vs 74.6%), strictly safer
    mid-game (the search really does decline gain>=1 cards; global
    zero would fine particles 50:1 via lik_floor on those).

SELECTED CANDIDATE (v10cand): DEFAULT_PF + tau_po=0.0 + eps=0.02.
Frozen-behavior checks green after every edit (anchors PASS;
sigma=0/nu=0/tau_po=tau_p/eps_out-no-op all reproduce champion
numbers exactly). New SoftOpponent params nu/sigma/discard_mode/
eps_out/tau_po all default-frozen; registry v6/v7 pins unaffected.
Phase B next: (a) truth-keyed reads, (b) held-out stream Brier +
random-mismatch, (c) fresh scenarios S4 (decline-type, free), S5
(take+discard, ~10 min), S6 (draw+discard, N=800).

